SUMMARY:Open Mic: A night to share bravely + connect deeply
DESCRIPTION:Event Type: Social\nOpen To: Members & Ticketed Guests\nTickets
 : Free for Members\, $20 for Guests\n\nhttps://www.eventbrite.com/e/open-m
 ic-a-night-to-share-bravely-connect-deeply-tickets-2003715278336?aff=oddtd
 tcreator\n\nABOUT THE EVENT:\n\nAn in-person open mic experience for coura
 geous humans to share creative work\, connect\, build community\, receive\
 , support\, and celebrate.\n\nLiberation Studio and Brave Enough present a
  casual\, fun night celebrating creative expression\, courage\, culture\, 
 identity\, and all the things that make us human. If you’ve got somethin
 g to share\, the spotlight is yours.\n\nBring a song\, story\, poem\, come
 dy\, dance\, family tradition\, cultural ritual\, work in progress\, hidde
 n talent\, or something else...passed down to you or dreamed up yesterday.
  Bring your roots\, history\, tender and meaningful things\, and things th
 at make you laugh. Share something you’ve practiced for years or try som
 ething for the first time.\n\nThere’s room for depth and play\, vulnerab
 ility and celebration\, the sacred and the silly. We don’t know all the 
 experiences that have shaped one another\, what we carry from our families
  and cultures\, or which parts of our identities rarely get a voice. This 
 is a space to bring those forward.\n\nYou don’t need to be polished or p
 erformance ready. Come practice being seen and heard\, play\, experiment\,
  take a risk\, be a little awkward\, and try something before you feel com
 pletely ready. If stepping up to the mic feels like a new edge\, you belon
 g here.\n\nWould you like to be a contributor and share on stage? If so\, 
 first register here as a "contributor" on Eventbrite. Then\, sign up here 
 by 11/20/26 and aim for around five minutes so there’s room for as many 
 shares as possible.\n\nThe evening will be acoustic\; you’re welcome to 
 bring your own instrument.\n\nCome to share\, witness\, play\, or practice
  taking up a little more space. If the stage isn’t calling you\, your en
 couragement\, curiosity\, energy\, and presence are just as much a part of
  the evening.\n\n___\n\nYour facilitators: Zannah Campora and Leigh Orne\n
 \nLeigh Orne is a celebration guide\, creativity coach\, and hype woman wh
 ose work centers connection: to self\, to others\, and to what wants to be
  born through you. She creates spaces that are playful\, intentional\, and
  deeply human.\n\nZannah Campora is a seasoned social entrepreneur who cre
 ates opportunities for connection & community that nurture inner and colle
 ctive liberation\, human-centric placemaking\, conscious business\, and co
 llaboration.\n\nInstructor: Leigh Orne & Zannah Campora\n\nPayment may be 
 required.\n\nPublicly listed\; guest eligibility and registration requirem
 ents vary. This is not an RSVP.\n\nhttps://share.fitdegree.com/?r=4359074
LOCATION:The Attic - Archipelago | 2345 7th Street
URL:https://share.fitdegree.com/?r=4359074
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
