SUMMARY:Denver Circling Night
DESCRIPTION:Event Type: Wellness/Social\nOpen To: Members & Ticketed Guests
 \nTickets: Free for the first 5 members\, $40 for guests\n\nOnly 5 free me
 mber spots\, first come first served. Once they're gone\, grab a guest tic
 ket here: https://coloradoconnectioncollective.com/events\n\nABOUT THE EVE
 NT:\n\nWhat if you could drop the small talk and experience conversations 
 that leave you feeling truly seen\, heard\, and understood? What if deep\,
  meaningful connection was something you could cultivate with anyone?\n\nT
 his gathering is an opportunity to step into a different way of relating\,
  one that brings clarity\, presence\, and profound connection. Through Cir
 cling® and authentic relating exercises\, we’ll slow down\, tune in\, a
 nd explore what it’s like to be fully ourselves in connection with other
 s.\n\nWHAT YOU MAY EXPERIENCE:\n• A deeper sense of presence and connect
 ion in your interactions\n• Conversations that move beyond the surface a
 nd into something real\n• The power of being fully seen and appreciated 
 just as you are\n• Insights into your own patterns in relationships\n•
  A shift in how you experience yourself and others\n\nJoin us every 2nd We
 dnesday and experience the kind of conversations that leave you feeling mo
 re alive\, connected\, and deeply understood.\n\nWe’ll be starting at 6:
 00 PM\, so we kindly ask that you arrive between 5:50 and 5:55 PM to get s
 ettled. To honor the experience for everyone\, doors will close at 6:10 PM
 .\n\nThis is an event facilitated by the Colorado Connection Collective in
  collaboration with Archipelago. \n\n_\n\nThe term “Circling®” is a r
 egistered trademark. We\, Mat Weddle and Jake Favor\, have licenses from T
 he International Circling Federation to use the term\, in accordance with 
 their guidelines\, in relation to the Circling facilitation we offer. We a
 re certified through The Circling Institute lineage. You can read about th
 e unique distinctions between the three lineages\, as well as the standard
 s of service required of licensees\, on the International Circling Federat
 ion website.\n\nInstructor: Colorado Connection Collective\n\nPayment may 
 be required.\n\nPublicly listed\; guest eligibility and registration requi
 rements vary. This is not an RSVP.\n\nhttps://share.fitdegree.com/?r=41972
 85
LOCATION:The Attic - Archipelago | 2345 7th Street
URL:https://share.fitdegree.com/?r=4197285
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
