SUMMARY:MatriMind for Entrepreneurs
DESCRIPTION:Event Type: Wellness/Social\nOpen To: Ticketed Members & Guests
 \n\nMember Tickets: $30 (only 5 available\, book here)\n\nGuest Tickets: $
 40\, purchase on Eventbrite: \nhttps://www.eventbrite.com/e/matrimind-for-
 business-owners-changemakers-tickets-2004096549729?aff=oddtdtcreator\n\nAB
 OUT THE EVENT:\n\nMatriMind is a monthly circle for curious\, purpose-driv
 en business owners exploring collaborative\, conscious ways of doing busin
 ess.\nMatriMind is a monthly drop-in collaborative mastermind circle for u
 p to 10 curious\, purpose-driven business owners exploring more conscious\
 , collaborative\, and regenerative ways of doing business.\nIt’s a wild 
 time. \n\nWhat if we could build thriving\, profitable businesses while mo
 ving beyond the patriarchal and extractive systems we’ve inherited and m
 aking our businesses human-centered\, collective-minded and standing for s
 ocial justice?\n\nThrough facilitated dialogue\, story sharing\, and colle
 ctive wisdom\, we support one another in navigating real business challeng
 es while reimagining what’s possible.\n\nTopics We’ll Explore\nBusines
 s Growth: Startups\, scaling\, revenue\, taxes\, marketing\, branding\, an
 d AI Leadership & Collaboration: Communication\, partnerships\, community 
 building\, and new leadership models\nRethinking Business: Matriarchy\, co
 nscious capitalism\, and regenerative business practices\n\nInner Liberati
 on: Deconditioning patriarchy and capitalism\, redefining success\, and al
 igning business with our values\nCome as you are\, with what you’re buil
 ding. Whether you’re launching\, growing\, pivoting\, or navigating a ch
 allenge\, you’ll find fresh perspectives\, meaningful connections\, and 
 collaborative support.\n\nThe Details\nFormat: Monthly drop-in mastermind\
 , maximum 10 participants\nWhen: Second Thursdays\, 10:30 AM–12:30 PM\nW
 here: The Attic at Archipelago\, Denver\nInvestment: $40 per gathering\, $
 30 for Arch members or $25 if funds are tight (because…we get it!)\nSpac
 e is limited! Register through Eventbrite here or Archipelago to claim you
 r spot.\n\nMeet Your Facilitator\, Zannah Campora\nZannah is a conscious e
 ntrepreneur\, certified coach\, facilitator\, community builder\, and Real
 tor passionate about business as a vehicle for social change.\n\nHer exper
 ience spans coaching\, community-building\, real estate\, hospitality\, ev
 ent production\, and social entrepreneurship. As the founder of Liberation
  Studio and co-owner of a wedding venue with her family\, she’s spent ye
 ars building businesses and communities rooted in connection\, collaborati
 on\, and purpose.\nHer work explores how we can cultivate more collaborati
 ve regenerative and human-centered ways of living and working.\n\nWhat Par
 ticipants Are Saying\n“I’ve been masterminding with Zannah for over a 
 year\, and I leave every conversation with a deep sense of clarity and ent
 husiasm for what’s next! Her wide-ranging business experience and genuin
 e love for identifying opportunities and working through challenges is a g
 ame changer.” -Leigh\n\n“I have genuinely felt so lit up by yall and r
 eally have expanded my heart to know I can truly follow my dreams\, so I a
 m doing the damn thing :)” -Ari\n\n“I’ve felt incredibly resourced b
 y this group and their wisdom. It’s been such an honor to support each o
 ther on our journeys of impact. We need so much more support than we could
  ever imagine to live these big\, brave lives we’re living.” -Melissa\
 n\nLet’s Reimagine Business Together\nMatriMind is an invitation to grow
  our businesses\, liberate ourselves from limiting systems\, and practice 
 more regenerative ways of building.\n\nBecause how we build matters just a
 s much as what we build. Let’s do it together!\n\nInstructor: Zannah Cam
 pora\n\nPayment may be required.\n\nPublicly listed\; guest eligibility an
 d registration requirements vary. This is not an RSVP.\n\nhttps://share.fi
 tdegree.com/?r=4360574
LOCATION:The Attic - Archipelago | 2345 7th Street
URL:https://share.fitdegree.com/?r=4360574
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
